# 📝 PDF to Question Paper Generator

Upload a PDF (notes, a chapter, a book) and get an exam-style question paper with
**MCQs, short questions and long questions**, plus an answer key.

**Stack:** Streamlit (UI) · Google Gemini `gemini-3.8-flash` (AI) · pypdf (PDF reading) · python-docx and reportlab (exports)

## Features
- Choose how many MCQs, short and long questions, and the marks for each
- Difficulty (Easy / Medium / Hard / Mixed) and optional topic focus
- Exam-style on-screen paper with school name, subject, time and total marks
- Download the paper and the answer key as **PDF** or **Word (.docx)**
- Answers can be shown or hidden on screen
- Scanned PDFs (no extractable text) are sent to Gemini directly
- Malformed AI output is filtered out, and you are warned if fewer questions than requested were produced

## Run locally
```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/<your-repo>.git
cd <your-repo>
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate   # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Get a free API key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey (it must be a **Google Gemini** key), then either:

- paste it into the app sidebar, **or**
- set an environment variable: `export GEMINI_API_KEY="your-key"` (Windows: `set GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key`), **or**
- create `.streamlit/secrets.toml` (never commit this file):
  ```toml
  GEMINI_API_KEY = "your-key"
  ```

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

## Configuration
| Name | Purpose | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | Gemini API key | none (sidebar prompt) |
| `GEMINI_MODEL` | Model to use | `gemini-3.8-flash` |

## Deploy on Streamlit Community Cloud
1. Push the files to a GitHub repo. `app.py`, `requirements.txt` and `README.md` must be in the **top level** with exactly these names.
2. Go to https://share.streamlit.io and sign in with GitHub.
3. Click **Create app**, choose the repo, branch `main`, main file `app.py`.
4. Open **Advanced settings → Secrets** and add: `GEMINI_API_KEY = "your-key"`
5. Click **Deploy**.

## Limitations
- Questions are AI-generated and can contain mistakes. Always review the paper and answer key.
- The PDF export uses built-in fonts, so it supports Latin-script text only. For Urdu, Arabic or other scripts, use the Word export.
- Maximum upload size is 10 MB.
- The PDF is sent to the Gemini API; check Google's data policy before uploading sensitive material.
- Gemini 3.8 Flash has introductory pricing until 31 Dec 2026; check the pricing page.
